// S441 reproducer — addendum-3 T5: a trailing `//` comment on a compound-state opener line breaks the compound.
// Compiler SHA: cf62b4154 (origin/main at dispatch)
// Command: bun compiler/bin/scrml.js compile docs/changes/s441-audit-gap-filing/repro/tut-compound-opener-trailing-comment.scrml --output-dir <scratch>
// Expected: compiles — §27.1 "`//` is a single-line comment. It is valid in all scrml contexts."
// Actual:   exit 1: `error [E-MARKUP-001]: `<form1>` is not a known HTML element and not a defined component…`
//           (stage NR) + `error [E-STATE-UNDECLARED]: bare `@form1` read with no reactive cell in scope…`.
//           Control: the identical file with the comment on its own line above the opener → exit 0.
<program>
<form1>   // the form's fields
    <title req> = <input type="text"/>
</>
<p>${@form1.isValid}</p>
<form1><title/></>
</program>
